 <h1>Exercise Name: Lying Dumbbell Tricep Extension / Dumbbell Skull Crusher</h1>
  <u><b><h4>Exercise Overview</h4></b></u>
  
This 3D anatomical visualization demonstrates the Lying Dumbbell Tricep Extension (Dumbbell Skull Crusher). The video highlights the triceps muscle (Triceps Brachii) in bright glowing colors, illustrating how bending and extending the arms at the elbow isolates the triceps on a flat bench while keeping the upper arms stable.

 Exercise Name: Lying Dumbbell Tricep Extension / Dumbbell Skull Crusher
 Target Muscles: Triceps Brachii (Long, Lateral, and Medial heads)
 Secondary Muscles: Forearms, Anterior Deltoids (for upper arm stabilization)

</div></div>

<h1>How to Perform (Step-by-Step)</h1>

<u><b><h4>Step 1: Setup</h4></b></u>
Lie flat on a bench with your feet planted firmly on the floor. Hold a dumbbell in each hand with a neutral grip (palms facing each other) and extend your arms straight up toward the ceiling.

<u><b><h4>Step 2: Alignment & Stability</h4></b></u>
Keep your upper arms stationary and perpendicular to your torso throughout the exercise.

<u><b><h4>Step 3: Lowering Phase (Eccentric)</h4></b></u>
Inhale as you slowly bend your elbows, lowering the dumbbells down toward the sides of your head/ears in a controlled arc without letting your upper arms drift forward or back.

<u><b><h4>Step 4: Extension Phase (Concentric)</h4></b></u>
Exhale as you press the dumbbells back up by extending your forearms straight until your triceps are fully contracted at the top position.



<h1>Key Benefits</h1>

 <b>◉Triceps Isolation:</b> Completely targets the back of the arms without letting the chest take over the movement.<br>
 
 <b>◉Joint-Friendly Wrist Position:</b> Using neutral-grip dumbbells allows for a natural range of motion, reducing strain on wrists and elbows compared to a straight barbell.<br>
 
 <b>◉Balanced Arm Development:</b> Using two separate dumbbells ensures both left and right triceps work equally without a dominant arm taking over.


<h1>Recommended Sets & Reps</h1>

| Goal | Sets | Reps | Rest |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Muscle Building (Hypertrophy) | 3 – 4 | 10 – 12 | 60 – 90 seconds |
| Endurance / Tone | 3 – 4 | 12 – 15 | 45 – 60 seconds |
| Strength | 3 – 4 | 8 – 10 | 90 seconds |

Keep your upper arms locked in place throughout the movement—only your forearms should move during each rep.


